{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"ed3735f9-d6da-4697-b328-f303098f1b69","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Cortex Eval Lab -- 3-Layer Eval Suite (M3, Lab 1a)\n\nRuns the **3-layer suite** on Cortex traces:\n- **Layer 1 -- Code**: deterministic regex/keyword check (free, instant)\n- **Layer 2 -- Safety**: mandated-refusal / confidential-leak gate (free, instant)\n- **Layer 3 -- Judge**: semantic LLM-as-Judge (needs `OPENAI_API_KEY`; falls back to a clearly-labeled MOCK heuristic if no key is set, so the notebook still runs top-to-bottom)\n\nEach layer returns `(caught: 1/0, reasoning: str)`. `caught=1` means the layer correctly flagged a bad prediction.","metadata":{}},{"id":"276cd1ad-af26-4128-8fd4-f3fd1de975b6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Layer 1 -- Code (deterministic)","metadata":{}},{"id":"5ec113dc-f39f-44be-a7a1-9160eb81a3c0","cell_type":"code","source":"pip install --upgrade \"openai>=1.0\"","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-25T08:27:58.695195Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-25T08:27:58.695503Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-25T08:28:10.350917Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-25T08:27:58.695467Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-25T08:28:10.349953Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Requirement already satisfied: openai>=1.0 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (2.32.0)\nCollecting openai>=1.0\n  Downloading openai-3.19.2-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (44 kB)\n\u001b[2K     \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m44.3/44.3 kB\u001